The testing was conducted by 10 users who had an interest in the medication reminder app concept.
Here are their summarised comments.


test prototype feedback:
Overall user friendly UI
Font was easy to read, sizing was good as well
Colors used were vibrant
Easy to understand layout
Pages looked very clean
Concept was really cool, it all looked very professional
Overall design was superb
Could have included instructions on each page for how to use functions
Font could have been a bit bigger
Layout looked optimized for Mobile, not sure about the layout for PC

final prototype feedback:
Pages were easy to navigate
Intractive and easy to use
Very well thought out and thorough layout, the page navigation was done smoothly allowing for quick and easy back and forth use between pages/functions
Functions were smooth, but pages felt like they lacked a bit of detail
Easy to use application design
Prototype showcased great initial functions
The pop up screen for the emergency contact, add contact was done really neatly
App layout still seems more optimized for mobile, should consider PC/web browser users as well
Overall very user friendly and easy to understand interface
Vibrant design, easy to use and navigate, layout and design made it seem easy to use for the intended purpose
